    "summary": "Goal: move the 3,458-line workflow.py into a standard-library package skills/ai-dev-workflow/scripts/aidw/ (layout from TARGET_ARCHITECTURE §3) with no behaviour change, keeping workflow.py as the entry point. Must keep: every CLI command, option, message, exit code and record format (golden + 147 tests); 'import workflow' and the names tests and tools use (main, build_parser, STAGES, find_secrets, decode_command_output, parse_analyzer, PY_CMD, REFERENCE, COMMIT_MODES, __version__, plus module attributes shutil and locale patched by two tests); prepublish_check.py loading workflow.py by file path; SKILL.md hooks running scripts/workflow.py; install.py copying the whole skill folder (aidw included). Pitfalls found: SKILL_DIR/TEMPLATES_DIR are computed from __file__ and change when code moves; section cross-references must form an acyclic import graph (hooks use status_line from the command helpers). Exclusions: no logic change, no renames of public names, no new features (engine API is F1.0.4, migrations/locking F1.0.5, version source F1.0.6). Affected: workflow.py, new aidw/ package, possibly pyproject.toml (mypy files)."
  },
